<title>GERMANY: Lower German sugar stocks offset by Oct output.</title>
<headline>Lower German sugar stocks offset by Oct output.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar carry-in stocks at the start of the new 1996/97 campaign on October 1 were 239,562 tonnes compared with 250,854 tonnnes a year earlier, whites value, monthly data from sugar industry association WVZ showed.</p>
<p>But stocks on Oct 31 were already 1.60 million tonnes against 1.34 million tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>They were boosted by a quick start to the September/January beet harvesting campaign, where October is the busiest month.</p>
<p>Roughly half of the total expected beet has already been processed, with domestic sugar production in October at 1.85 million compared with 1.55 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Oct/Sept 1995/96 total output had been 3.83 million.</p>
<p>WVZ also gave further monthly details in tonnes --</p>
<p>					   Oct 96		Oct 95</p>
<p>    Imports			    9,808		 16,456</p>
<p>    Exports			  222,059		203,868</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar sales	 272,887		267,435</p>
<p>-- Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
